Hi [USER] , thanks for filing this issue! I was able to confirm that this is an issue in Streamlit OSS, not just Streamlit Community Cloud. I was able to repro it locally with an app that sets query string params. 

A simple repro app:

```py
import streamlit as st

st.checkbox("Toggle this")

st.query_params["number"] = 1
```

Toggle the checkbox, and you'll note that each re-run of this app will (erroneously) push a new state to the browser history. This happens in this piece of code: https://github.com/streamlit/streamlit/blob/develop/frontend/app/src/App.tsx#L787-L797

To fix this, I'm pretty sure this logic should be updated to check that the URL is actually different before updating state, so the bug fix might look something like this:

```ts
  handlePageInfoChanged = (pageInfo: PageInfo): void => {
    const { queryString } = pageInfo

    const url = new URL(document.location.href)
    url.search = queryString || ""
    const targetUrl = url.toString()

    // Only send URL updates if the URL has changed
    if (targetUrl !== document.location.href) {
      return
    }

    window.history.pushState({}, "", targetUrl)

    this.hostCommunicationMgr.sendMessageToHost({
      type: "SET_QUERY_PARAM",
      queryParams: queryString ? `?${queryString}` : "",
    })
  }
```

I will work with the team to get a proper fix for this, but wanted to confirm that this is an issue and thank you again for filing it!
